# Editor swap files
*.kate-swp

# Scratch staging (agent work product; the durable artifacts are in
# dotfiles-ai/dsh and the plan/checklist files, not here)
scratch/

# Build-only output that must NOT ship: rebuilt locally via
# `pnpm build` / the `prepare` script. node_modules/ and coverage/ stay ignored.
node_modules/
coverage/

# The bundle artifacts below ARE committed on purpose. aidos is installed
# from git (github:), and the package manager blocks git-hosted install-time
# builds until allowBuilds is configured, so lib/client.js,
# dist/host/aidos-plugin.js and presets/aidos/aidos-tools.js must ship from
# the repo instead of being generated at install time.
#
# THE RULE (#148): a commit that touches src/ ships its rebuild. Run
# `node build.mjs` and commit the artifacts it writes, in the same commit as
# the source change. These files are not by-products — they are the product,
# and src/ is only their input.
#
# This is enforced, not remembered: build.mjs records a digest of every
# source plus its own recipe in lib/build-manifest.json, and
# tests/u148-bundle-freshness.test.ts fails the normal suite run when the
# two sides disagree in either direction. It exists because the rule WAS
# only remembered, and the shipped client bundle silently fell twelve
# commits behind src/ — four tickets' worth of work absent from the artifact
# consumers install, while every test stayed green.

